cb","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3wJRTNCBsvS0u0NrWJwcb"}},{"id":"879946","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"880987","description":"Lower Blue Run In September 2011","caption":"Late summer flows","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Chad Stone","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879946","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879946"}},{"id":"40144","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5600","description":"","caption":"Lower Blue River","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/40144","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/40144"}},{"id":"885518","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"888329","description":"clear, cold water and beautiful scenery on the Lower Blue","caption":"Scenic Lower Blue","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"cupcake","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/885518","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/885518"}},{"id":"885519","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"888330","description":"after roping boats down to the put in","caption":"Class V put in ","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"cupcake","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/885519","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/885519"}},{"id":"i1UaW64sci87ZcG6JhTSG","ext":"jpg","post_id":"i1UaW64sci87ZcG6JhTSG","description":"","caption":"The put in","poi_name":null,"subject":"The put in","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2018-09-15T08:45:00.000Z","updated_at":"2022-06-04T14:46:42.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/i1UaW64sci87ZcG6JhTSG","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/i1UaW64sci87ZcG6JhTSG"}},{"id":"885520","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"888331","description":"the first of two fishing weirs on this stretch. when in doubt, scout it out!","caption":"Weir number 1","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/885520","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/885520"}},{"id":"885521","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"888332","description":"as you approach the take out you will start to see houses on river right and cows on river left ","caption":"Lower Blue","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"cupcake","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/885521","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/885521"}},{"id":"885517","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"888328","description":"April HIllman getting some surf action on the Lower Blue","caption":"Lower Blue","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"cupcake","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/885517","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/885517"}}],"detail":{"id":"363","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"The Lower Blue is dam affected. The rapids are all Class III pool drop or boulder piles. Most of the rapids are fairly short but a few can be long and are unpleasant to swim. The last drop after leaving the shadow of Green Mountain is a stair stepping flume on the left with a small hole. This is a gentle whitewater run for most Colorado boaters. Shuttle is easy. Put in at the base of the dam on 30 RD off Hwy 9 and drive back out to HWY 9 go left then take the next left and park where the river and road meet. A rope is recommended to lower boats down the hill for the normal put in.\n\nThe run breaks down into some wave trains with various spots to play. The largest is called the Canyon Wall rapid which is shortly followed up by two small diversion dams. At low flows it is recommended to portage the dams unless you don't like your boat. They are easy to scout with large pools on either side but a river right portage is best. Around normal flows they can be a fun rapid with surf waves at times. Make sure not to miss the takeout at the bridge.","averageGradient":"49","maxGradient":null,"length":"4","correlations":[{"reachID":"363","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":"Optimal flow is 1500 CFS (flows based on 2012 WFET Colorado Basin Report). ","highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"299","beginMediumRunnable":"1400","beginHighRunnable":"1600","endHighRunnable":"10000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"BLUE RIVER BELOW GREEN MOUNTAIN RESERVOIR, CO","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"09057500","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"64","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"2.51","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"39.88026354","longitude":"-106.3339175"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/09057500","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/09057500/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":"Previous Flowbands: \nRange of Boatable Flows (R0-R9): 299 - 10000 cfs  Comment: \t\tRange of acceptable flows - no maximum flow suggested for non-commercial boating (flows based on 2012 WFET Colorado Basin Report). \r\n\r\n\r\n\nMedium Runnable (R4-R6): 1400 - 1600 cfs  Comment: Optimal flow is 1500 CFS (flows based on 2012 WFET Colorado Basin Report). \n\nMigrat